course: dictionary
lesson: 11758
title: Banning: when a rule says no
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Banning means officially saying that something is not allowed. Think of a rule written down by people in charge, like a school or a council. «The school is banning phones in class from next term.» The word from next term tells you this is a decision for the future, and the school is in charge of it.
explain: Banning comes from the word ban, and -ing shows the action is happening or the act itself is being named. When it is a verb, it works like a doing word: «The council is banning plastic bags.» When it is a noun, it names the act: «The banning of plastic bags helped the beach.» Both mean the same idea: forbidding something.
explain: Look for clues around banning. Words like officially, council, rule, or law often show that someone in charge has made the decision. Words like from, in, or on tell you what is banned and where. «The club is banning Sam from the pool for one week» means Sam is not allowed in the pool for that time.
fact: Ban means to officially say that something is not allowed.
fact: Banning is the -ing form of ban, and it can be a verb or a noun.
fact: «Banning someone from» a place means they are not allowed to go there.
fact: «The banning of» something names the act of forbidding it.
fact: A good check is to swap in not allowed: «The school is not allowing phones in class» should still make sense.
exercise: «The school is banning phones in class from next term.» What does banning mean here? | Giving every pupil a free phone | *Officially saying phones are not allowed | Taking a photo of the class | Painting the phones bright colours
exercise: Which word in «The council is banning plastic bags in shops.» is a clue that this is an official decision? | *council | shops | plastic | bags
exercise: In «The banning of plastic bags helped the beach», what does banning mean? | The act of cleaning the beach | The act of buying plastic bags | The act of making bags from plastic | *The act of forbidding plastic bags
test: «The club is banning Sam from the pool for one week.» What does banning Sam from the pool mean? | *Officially saying Sam is not allowed in the pool | Sam is given a free pool pass | Sam is swimming very fast | Sam is teaching others to swim
test: Which word is the -ing form of ban? | bang | bans | banned | *banning
exam: A news report says «The government is banning a dangerous toy from every shop.» What does banning tell you? | The toy is being sold at a lower price | The shops have made the toy themselves | The government is giving the toy away to every shop | *The government has officially said the toy is not allowed in shops
